    "media:imagetext": "- 2 -\nAfter Myra and the baby left, I had Shirley home for a month.\nWe spent a lot of time sewing• Shirley made two dresses, with my\nhelp, and I made two.\nOne a navy blue sheer wool, which I am very\npleased with.\nThe other, a print, I am not too sure about. I haven't\nworn it yet,\nas it doesn't look just like the victure did. Before\nShirley went back, Angela was quite sick.\nI spent as much time with\nher as I could.\nHer cousin and I took turns.\nShe finally had a nurse\nduring the day, and I stayed with her at nights.\nThe doctor wanted\nher to go to the hospital, but she didn't want to. She had pneumonia.\nShe is quite all right now. Myra has had bronchitas for the last\ntwo weeks, and I have been going over there in the daytime. Mrs.\nKlaus has kept Joelle. I am going over this afternoon. Yesterday\nI went over and took her to the doctor and she seemed to feel a\nlittle better. She went back to work last Tuesday,\nbut had to stop\non Thursday.\nThe doctor is giving her oromizen, (I don't know how to\nspell it,, and it seems to be helping her.\nI went with Bee Hatie the other night to see Lowell Thomas'\npictures of Tibet.\nThey were so interesting, and in the end they\ngave F.A.A. quite a bit of advertising.\nHave you seen it? I am afraid\nthat is the way I am going to do my traveling.\nI am so glad you are\nhaving such a wonderful trip, and everything has turned out as you\nhad hoped it would.\nThat was interesting about Clarance Young. I thought he was\nOff P. A. A• I heard that he resigned because he thought he wasn't\nbeing treated right.\nI was so sorry to hear about the Bonds. I had some friends\nto luncheon the other day, among them was Mrs. Kroll, who always\nspeake to kindly about Harold and Mr. Bond.\nHarold and re\nShe is very nice.\nI had Pat Taggart, who asked to be rememberedto yo when I wrote,\nNellie Sharp and Mercedes Me Micking, and Angela, and two others\nwhom you don't know.\nThey all seemed to be so congenial, and it\nwas all very pleasant. I was so far behind as I have been rather\ntied down the last few months.\nI have a wonderful gadget I want to send. you when you get\nsettled at home. It is a dispenser for hand cream, and just gives\none the proper amount.\nIt is like a cole cream jar,\nand is not\nbad looking. I have one in my bedroom and one in the kitchen.\nI must leave you. I don't know whether this will ever catch\nup with you. I am so sorry I didn't get it written before you left\nParis.\nDearest love to you and Hebe, and very best wishes to\nHarold. You have more than paid me back for anything we ever\ndid for you.\nI can't tell you how much my visit with you meant\nto me. I just forgot everything, and enjoyed every minute with\nyou, besides all the wonderful shows. I think of it all, most\nevery day. I do love you all very much.\nAs ever,\nelma.\nPane thank the for her lite. Spange\nd RAID SIE\nte test yes shine you like his ring he",
